I inverted the bounds test into a likely-true fast path and added branch-prediction hints so the common valid lookup falls through to the array load instead of taking the invalid-return branch.

```cpp
FIT_UINT8 Field::GetNum(void) const
{
    if (__builtin_expect(profile != NULL, 1) &&
        __builtin_expect(profileIndex < profile->numFields, 1))
        return profile->fields[profileIndex].num;
    return FIT_FIELD_NUM_INVALID;
}
```